e":"Bavarian","termine":"spechtln","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmh","nome":"Middle High German","termine":"spēhen","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*spehōn","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*spehōną","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*speḱ-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Bavarian spechtln, from Middle High German spēhen (“to watch, peer, peek”), from Old High German spehōn, spiohōn, from Proto-West Germanic *spehōn, from Proto-Germanic *spehōną (“to see, look”), from Proto-Indo-European *speḱ- (“to look”). Doublet of spähen."},{"parola":"Wappler","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly","significato":"idiot, fool, incompetent person","termine_origine":"Wappler","catena":[{"codice":"bar","nome":"Bavarian","termine":"Wappler","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmh","nome":"Middle High German","termine":"wabelen","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"gmh","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Bavarian Wappler, possibly from wappeln (“to move unsteady, shakily”), from a variant of Middle High German wabelen (“to move about”). Compare wabbeln."}]}